---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
    title="WiFi FTP Server Privacy Policy - LogicPath Systems"
    description="Privacy Policy for WiFi FTP Server by LogicPath Systems. Last updated 28 October 2026."
>
    <section class="legal-page" style="padding-top: 120px; min-height: 100vh;">
        <div class="container reveal">
            <div class="glass-card" style="padding: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);">
                <header style="margin-bottom: 3rem; text-align: center;">
                    <h1 class="gradient-text">Privacy Policy</h1>
                    <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>WiFi FTP Server</strong></p>
                    <p style="color: var(--text-secondary);"><strong>Last updated:</strong> 28 October 2026</p>
                </header>

                <main class="legal-content">
                    <h2>In short</h2>
                    <p>WiFi FTP Server lets you open your phone's files from a computer on the same Wi-Fi: in File Explorer or Finder (as a network drive), in an FTP app or in a web browser. It works without an account.</p>
                    <p>Your files go directly between your phone and your computer over your own network. They are never sent to us or to any cloud service, and we never see their names or contents.</p>
                    <p>The app uses two Google services: AdMob, to show ads, and Firebase Analytics, to count which features are used. Both collect some device data, as described below. We do not sell personal data.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>Permissions and why they are needed</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>All files access (MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE):</strong> the core of the app is sharing the phone's storage with your computer like a network drive. It needs this to list every folder and to copy, rename, move and delete files when you do so from the computer. It is requested only after an explanation, and you can turn it off at any time in Android settings.</li>
                        <li><strong>Internet, network state and local network access:</strong> used to run the FTP, WebDAV (network drive) and browser servers on your Wi-Fi while you have the server on, and by AdMob and Firebase Analytics.</li>
                        <li><strong>Wi-Fi multicast (CHANGE_WIFI_MULTICAST_STATE):</strong> lets the phone hear and answer computers on your Wi-Fi that look it up by its name, as described below. Used only while the server is on.</li>
                        <li><strong>Foreground service, notifications and wake locks:</strong> while the server is on, a "Server on" notification keeps it running with the screen off or the app closed, and keeps Wi-Fi awake for copies. It stops as soon as you turn the server off, from the app, the notification or the Quick Settings tile.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>Your files and what stays on your phone</h2>
                    <p>Files are only reachable while you have the server turned on, only from your local network, and only by someone who has the sign-in details shown in the app. By default the app makes a random user name, password and browser code once and keeps them, so a computer can save them; you can choose new ones every time the server is turned on instead. Read-only mode lets computers open and copy files without changing them.</p>
                    <p>While the server is on, the phone answers to a name on your local network, such as wififtp-k3m9.local, and announces its FTP and WebDAV servers there (mDNS), so a saved drive keeps working when the router gives the phone a new address. The name is made at random once on the phone; it contains nothing about you or your device. These announcements stay on your Wi-Fi and stop when the server is turned off.</p>
                    <p>The Activity list (sign-ins, copies and changes, with file names and the computer's local network address) is saved on the phone for 30 days so you can look back at it. You can clear it at any time, or turn saving off on the Options tab so it is kept only while the app is open. It is never sent anywhere.</p>
                    <p>The app keeps its settings, including a fixed sign-in if you set one, in a private file inside the app. For FTPS it makes its own encryption certificate on the phone and keeps it there too. Uninstalling the app deletes them.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>Advertising (Google AdMob)</h2>
                    <p>The app shows ads from Google AdMob: a banner at the end of the Server screen; an app open ad that may appear while the app opens or when you come back to it after a while (not the first time you open the app, and not when you return from Android settings or the share menu); and an occasional full-screen ad after you turn the server off at the end of a session in which files were copied or changed. Full-screen ads are at least 4 minutes apart.</p>
                    <p>To show and measure ads, Google may collect your device's advertising ID, IP address, approximate location, device and app information, and how you interact with ads.</p>
                    <p>In the European Economic Area, the UK and Switzerland you are asked for consent first, and you can change your choice at any time in Options &rarr; Privacy choices. Elsewhere you can turn off personalised ads, and reset or delete your advertising ID, in Android settings.</p>
                    <p>How Google uses this data: <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a></p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>Usage statistics (Firebase Analytics)</h2>
                    <p>To learn which features are used and to fix problems, the app sends anonymous usage events to Google Firebase Analytics: which screens are opened, when the server is turned on or off and for how long, how many files were copied each way, which way a computer connected (FTP, drive or browser), and which options are chosen.</p>
                    <p>Firebase also records an app instance ID created for this install, the device model, Android and app version, language, first open and session times, and an approximate location (country or region) worked out from the IP address.</p>
                    <p>The statistics never include file or folder names, file contents, network addresses of your devices, user names, passwords or codes. The advertising ID is not collected by Firebase Analytics in this app, and the statistics are not used for advertising.</p>
                    <p>You can turn this off at any time in Options &rarr; Share usage statistics. Google keeps the event data for no longer than 14 months. How Google handles this data: <a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy</a></p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>Children</h2>
                    <p>The app is not directed at children under 13 and does not knowingly collect data from them.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
                    <p>To remove everything the app stored on your phone, uninstall it or clear its storage in Android settings. Usage statistics are linked only to the app instance ID, which is deleted with the app; to stop sending them, turn off Options &rarr; Share usage statistics. For data Google holds for ads, use your Google account and Android ad settings.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
                    <p>If this policy changes, the new version will be published in the app and on its web page with a new date.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
                    <p>WiFi FTP Server is an independent app. It is not made by or affiliated with Google, Android, Microsoft, Apple or FileZilla.</p>
                    <p>Files deleted, moved or overwritten from a computer are changed on the phone straight away. There is no recycle bin, so check before you delete, or turn on read-only mode.</p>
                    <p>Plain FTP, WebDAV and the browser page are not encrypted; FTPS is. Use them on networks you trust, such as your home Wi-Fi or this phone's hotspot.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>Contact</h2>
                    <p>LogicPath Systems &middot; <a href="mailto:contact@logicpathsystems.com" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">contact@logicpathsystems.com</a></p>
                </main>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</Layout>

<style>
    .legal-content h2 {
        color: var(--text-primary);
        margin-top: 2.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
        font-size: 1.5rem;
    }

    .legal-content h3 {
        color: var(--text-primary);
        margin-top: 1.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
        font-size: 1.25rem;
    }

    .legal-content p, .legal-content ul {
        color: var(--text-secondary);
        margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
        font-size: 1.05rem;
        line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .legal-content ul {
        padding-left: 2rem;
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    .legal-content li {
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }
</style>
